{"t": 1794116946.7233012, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "Heads-up: this change introduced a production reconciliation bug.\n\nSentry issue LEDGER-WORKER-9A \u2014 \"ReconciliationMismatch: converted totals off by 1 minor unit (expected 1100, got 1099)\" \u2014 first seen in release ledger-worker@2026.11.3, 2,201 events, still unresolved.\nhttps://acme.sentry.io/issues/LEDGER-WORKER-9A/\n\nReplacing Decimal rounding with `int()` truncates the fractional minor unit (e.g. 1099.6 -> 1099) instead of rounding to the nearest minor unit, which breaks reconciliation. Fix in worker/rates.py restores `Decimal(...).quantize(Decimal(\"1\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_UP)`; with the fix the reported case converts to 1100.", "issue_number": 412, "owner": "acme", "repo": "ledger-worker"}, "ok": true}
